From cc5661cba81f14ea7ca0b1d31fe6d503b3c5c474 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Bates <help@batesai.org>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:59:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Google sign-in: optional return_to so other pages can get
 members back

GET /api/auth/oauth/google?return_to=<path> remembers a validated
same-site path in a ten-minute HttpOnly cookie (oauth_return_to), because
Google's redirect_uri is fixed at /membership and cannot carry it. The
/membership callback then lands on <path>?signed_in=1 after a successful
exchange, or <path>?signin_error=<reason> on failure, and clears the
cookie. First user: Subject Mastery (/subjectmastery/).

Accepted paths: one leading "/", only [A-Za-z0-9/_.-], no "//", no
backslash, no "." or ".." segment, at most 200 characters, not under
/api/ or /cdn-cgi/. Anything else is ignored. The cookie is re-validated
on read, since a sibling *.batesai.org host could plant one.

Without the cookie every response from both routes is unchanged
(checked header-for-header against 7eea212f with a stubbed token
exchange); DaemonManager's sign-in webview still sees
/membership/?signed_in=1. Apple's form_post path is untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
